# Reference data are compared byte for byte against what NJOY2016 and other
# codes wrote, so git must never convert their line endings. A Windows
# checkout turned LF into CRLF and broke two byte-exact ACE tests on the CI
# Windows runner (gh #862, 2026-10-14).
reference-data/** -text

# kovan's schema-compatibility and signing fixtures are pinned byte for byte
# (a stored file must load and write back unchanged; a signature covers exact
# bytes), so git must never convert their line endings either. Git for
# Windows' `core.autocrlf = true` turned them CRLF and failed eight tests on
# the CI Windows runner (2026-10-22). The kovan schema page is in the list
# because `schema_743.rs` round-trips the examples it shows.
crates/kovan/tests/fixtures/** -text
crates/kovan-common/tests/data/** -text
crates/kovan-common/tests/fixtures/** -text
crates/kovan-common/src/review/signing/fixtures/** -text
docs/site/kovan-schema/index.html -text
